-- title:
--   A G_q-stable inertia-fixed level has degree at most f
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and let $\mathcal O =$ `OO q` denote the valuation subring [`padicIntegers q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) of the algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb Q}_q$ (the valuation subring of its canonical $\mathbb R_{\ge 0}$-valued valuation), with residue field $\bar\kappa =$ `kbar q`, and let `GG q` be the group of $\mathbb Q_q$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_q$. Let $K_w$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_q/\mathbb Q_q$ which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q_q$, and write $R_w =$ `Rw q Kw` for the valuation subring of $K_w$ obtained by pulling back $\mathcal O$ along $K_w \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}_q$, and $\mathrm{res}_w$ for the map sending $x \in R_w$ to the residue in $\bar\kappa$ of its image in $\mathcal O$. Assume: (i) every $g \in$ `GG q` maps $K_w$ into itself; (ii) every $w \in$ `GG q` with the property that $w\cdot x - x$ lies in the non-units of $\mathcal O$ for all $x \in \mathcal O$ (so that $w$ is trivial on $\bar\kappa$) fixes every element of $K_w$; and (iii) there is a natural number $f > 0$ with $\mathrm{res}_w(x)^{q^f} = \mathrm{res}_w(x)$ for all $x \in R_w$. Then $[K_w : \mathbb Q_q] =$ `Module.finrank ℚ_[q] Kw` is at most $f$.
--
--   This is the Galois-theoretic half of the statement that for an unramified finite subextension of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_q/\mathbb Q_q$ the degree is bounded by the residue degree: the inertia hypothesis forces the Galois group of $K_w$ to be generated by Frobenius, whose order is bounded by $f$. It is used in the construction of a ramified character of inertia at $q$, via the assertion that some inertia element moves $q^{1/p}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ExtCitation_LocalLevel_finrank_le_of_forall_resw_pow_eq.lean

